Package: mqtt-exec-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Jason Milen <jpmilen@gmail.com>
Depends: systemd
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: Run locally-configured commands when triggered over MQTT
 Subscribes to one or more MQTT topics, each mapped in a local config file to a
 fixed, pre-defined command. An incoming MQTT message only ever selects which
 already-configured action runs -- it can never supply the command itself, so
 this stays safe to trigger from network/MQTT even for privileged actions like
 restarting a systemd unit.
 .
 Publishes Home Assistant MQTT-discovery config for each configured action, so a
 matching button entity appears in HA automatically with no manual YAML/dashboard
 setup required.
 .
 Ships a self-contained Python runtime under /opt/mqtt-exec-agent, built with uv;
 no system Python version or network access is required at install time.
